\ A raise inside a word called from a quotation that a prelude combinator runs. The `choose`
\ call is top-level, so it stays interpreted under eager and one golden binds both suites.
\
\ The `boom` row is the pinned shape: its frame is pushed while the quotation's body runs, so
\ its source is the quotation's file, not the prelude file `choose` was defined in. `5 drop`
\ keeps the call out of tail position, where the frame would be elided.

boom: [ 1 "x" + ] ;

1 2 [ boom 5 drop ] choose
